        ],
        "en": [
          "Three events are documented in the sources (construction c. 1730, new shingles 1781, roof repair 1903); the other stages are modelled weathering of the timber, spread between those dates. The same processes act throughout: greying from sun and rain (faster on the south and west), slower darkening of sheltered parts, algae and moss from the north, and darkening near the ground from splash water."
        ]
